{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 40, :comments ["<b>The sense of</b> ואלה שמות אלופי עשו למקומתם [and these are the names of the chiefs of Esau by their places] — they have known places to this day, and these are the words of Moses, and those mentioned are the sons of the chiefs written above, and he mentioned only one who has a place:" "<b>Timna.</b> In this place it is masculine, for we have many names identical for masculine and feminine, and likewise אהליבמה [Oholibamah]. Or the explanation is that there is an additional chief, and it is Chief Timna who was the concubine of Eliphaz — אלה הם אלופיה עלוה גם יתת [these are her chiefs, Alvan also and Jetheth], and these are the chiefs of Amalek, and the chiefs of Oholibamah were seven in the days of Moses, men of places; therefore he added to specify במושבותם [in their settlements]:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {1 "I read לבאר as 'to specify/clarify'; the phrase ואלופי אהליבמה הי׳ שבעה echoes Gen 36:36 counting seven Horite chiefs but the identification with Oholibamah's line is Ibn Ezra's own inference."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:47:13.300000597Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}